  "notes": [
    "Compare arms within the same study and case only. Do not pool different study baselines.",
    "Native includes existing context packs and the normal verification route.",
    "Times are milliseconds; phase durations overlap. Costs are provider-rate estimates in USD, not invoices.",
    "Main-treatment appends source to eligible main search results, with eight augmentation attempts per session; model lookups are not capped.",
    "Uncapped exploratory variants remove augmentation attempt/match/source-count caps, while byte budgets and deadlines remain. The main-only screen still has its earlier augmentation allowance.",
    "Screens change different stages; the shard screen changes both main and compliance grouping. One observation per configuration is not an adoption test.",
    "Search-recognition changes command eligibility; slim-compliance changes only page-specific scoped rule delivery.",
    "Private PR code and full transcripts are not public. This sanitized export supports arithmetic checks, not independent bug adjudication or full replay.",
    "Observed supported concerns are not complete ground truth. No complete recall or independent blind evaluation is claimed.",
    "The earlier compliance-ablation treatment disables compliance only, with the normal main-prompt omitted-guidance scheduling notice. Main and verification remain native. It was not adopted; all six runs missed the predefined concern.",
    "Exact diff sizes, private finding details and internal report identifiers are omitted."
